<title>PHILIPPINES: BPI converts some preferred to common shrs.</title>
<headline>BPI converts some preferred to common shrs.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of the Philippine Islands (BPI) said  on Friday 53.873 million of its preferred A shares were converted  into common stocks.</p>
<p>BPI told the Philippine Stock Exchange the converted common shares  held by two major shareholders, will form part of the listed BPI shares  in the market.</p>
<p>Ayala Corp had converted 42.899 million preferred shares, while JP  Morgan Overseas Capital Corp, 10.974 million shares.</p>
<p>The new common shares form 8.6 percent of the BPI's total 621.095  million outstanding common shares.</p>
<p>BPI closed one peso higher at 152 pesos on Friday.</p>
<p>-- Manila Newsroom (63 2) 841-8938 Fax 817-6267</p>
